+    <section anchor="overview" numbered="false" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-unnumbered-1">
+      <name slugifiedName="name-overview">Overview</name>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-unnumbered-1-1">This document describes in detail the definition of TIFF-F that is
+used to store facsimile images.  The TIFF-F encoding has been
+folklore with no standard reference definition before this document.</t>
+    </section>
+    <section anchor="internet-fax-working-group" numbered="false" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-unnumbered-2">
+      <name slugifiedName="name-internet-fax-working-group">Internet Fax Working Group</name>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-unnumbered-2-1">This document is a product of the IETF Internet Fax Working Group.
+All comments on this document should be forwarded to the email
+distribution list at &lt;ietf-fax@imc.org&gt;.</t>
+    </section>
+    <section anchor="abstract-1" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-1">
+      <name slugifiedName="name-abstract-1">Abstract</name>
       <t indent="0" pn="section-1-1">This document references the Tag Image File Format (TIFF) to define
 the F profile of TIFF for facsimile (TIFF-F) as a file format that
 may be used for the storage and interchange of facsimile images.</t>
